  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chongqing-Dadukou Fiscal Sustainability DPO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Chongqing-Dadukou District Development Policy Financing (DPF) supports Chongqing-Dadukou District Government in achieving fiscal sustainability through a forward-looking, comprehensive and transparent public finance framework that integrates budget, public investment and debt management. The DPF program in Dadukou is divided into three pillars: fiscal sustainability, integrated capital investment plan, and transparency. Under this operation, Dadukou can serve as a pilot for local government fiscal reform in China by creating a forward-looking, comprehensive and transparent public finance regime that integrates budget, public investment and debt management. While this is the first subnational development policy operation in China, the project design is informed by the experience of such subnational operations in other countries, as well as from other types of operations in China.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This DPL operation is aimed at assisting the Chongqing Municipal Government in the adjustment to the new Budget Law that promises to limit subnational borrowing going forward and achieve fiscal sustainability. The majority of finance in China is at the lowest (district) level of Government.  Thus, the achievement of fiscal sustainability in Chongqing Municipality is thus inseparable from the effective monitoring and regulation of district finances.  Chongqing has chosen Daduko district as a pilot district for the focus of this operation, which will support the transition to a new model of incentives and contraints to ensure the success and financial sustainability at the district level.  This will involve specific PFM reforms, including a fiscally sustainable MTFF and 3-year rolling budget in Daduko District.</narrative>
  </description>
